    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that owner responses include a `bulkSignupWarning` flag: `true` once more than 80 owners have already been created on the current business day, `false` otherwise. The acceptance test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges, each kept to a single responsibility:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` (readOnly `boolean`) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field with a getter/setter.\n\n2. **New `BulkSignupWarningEvaluator`** (`rest/signup/`) \u2014 A small component that owns the warning rule: count owners registered on today's business day and compare against a threshold of 80. It reuses the existing `ClinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn(...)` and `BusinessDay.onOrAfter(...)`, so it counts owners under the exact business day newly created owners are stored under \u2014 the same accumulation path as the daily-limit rule.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 Marked `bulkSignupWarning` as ignored in `toOwnerDto`, since it's derived from clinic-wide state (DB count + current date), not from the owner's own fields.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 Injected the evaluator and added a private `toOwnerDto(Owner)` helper that maps and stamps the current warning, used by both `getOwner` and `addOwner` so single-owner responses carry the flag without duplicating logic.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nOne scoping decision worth flagging: I set the flag on the single-owner responses (`addOwner`, `getOwner`) that the spec and test target, and left the list/page endpoints unchanged. If you'd like the warning surfaced on the collection endpoints too, that's a small follow-up.",
